{"term":"event","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f32899ed924792ed74","definition":"An occurrence; something that happens.","example":"In the event of strong wind…","pos":"noun","synonyms":["circumstance"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:07ea78c65c62fb9749","definition":"A prearranged social activity (function, etc.)","example":"I went to an event in San Francisco last week.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:47ce8d573fa684faad","definition":"One of several contests that combine to make up a competition.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d234247030a052bb53","definition":"An end result; an outcome (now chiefly in phrases).","example":"hard beginnings have many times prosperous events […].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7cece37b5230bade62","definition":"A remarkable person.","example":"Miss Burton, you are an event! Sleepy, old Lymston's going to love you! Bye-bye. Bye.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sensation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, figuratively, uncommon","register":"dated, figuratively, uncommon","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cc312d4e9d2348a450","definition":"A point in spacetime having three spatial coordinates and one temporal coordinate.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f1524ff71b2f4c831","definition":"A possible action that the user can perform that is monitored by an application or the operating system (event listener). When an event occurs an event handler is called which performs a specific task.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e84470f0904c13f89","definition":"A set of some of the possible outcomes; a subset of the sample space.","example":"If X is a random variable representing the toss of a six-sided die, then its sample space could be denoted as {1,2,3,4,5,6}. Examples of events could be: X=1, X=2, X>5,X̸=4, and X isin 1,3,5.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:142347d3977577ca2d","definition":"An affair in hand; business; enterprise.","example":"Leave we him to his events.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fc6d2a734d88514efd","definition":"An episode of severe health conditions.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b456a9ae64a54bf793","definition":"To occur, take place.","example":"1590, Robert Greene, Greene’s Never Too Late, in The Life and Complete Works in Prose and Verse of Robert Greene, Volume 8, Huff Library, 1881, p. 33,\n[…] I will first rehearse you an English Historie acted and evented in my Countrey of England […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dbfdb60a67e0fa301e","definition":"To be emitted or breathed out; to evaporate.","example":"c. 1597, Ben Jonson, The Case is Altered, Act V, Scene 8, in C. H. Herford and Percy Simpson (editors), Ben Jonson, Volume 3, Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1927, p. 178,\nô that thou sawst my heart, or didst behold\nThe place from whence that scalding sigh evented.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:02ea978f106931774f","definition":"To expose to the air, ventilate.","example":"1559, attributed to William Baldwin, “How the Lorde Clyfford for his straunge and abhominable cruelty came to as straunge and sodayne a death” in The Mirror for Magistrates, Part III, edited by Joseph Haslewood, London: Lackington, Allen & Co., 1815, Volume 2, p. 198,\nFor as I would my gorget have undon\nTo event the heat that had mee nigh undone,\nAn headles arrow strake mee through the throte,\nWhere through my soule forsooke his fylthy cote.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪˈvɛnt/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/89/En-us-event.ogg/En-us-event.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["event horizon","in the event","wise after the event"]}